    "sha": "825d9c193a40c050779baef38a1cc17d596ae23c",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOV5OD-doAKDgyNWQ5YzE5M2E0MGMwNTA3NzliYWVmMzhhMWNjMTdkNTk2YWUyM2M",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "dylanoliverdo-coder",
        "email": "265406556+dylanoliverdo-coder@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-26T05:49:14Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "dylanoliverdo-coder",
        "email": "265406556+dylanoliverdo-coder@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-26T05:49:14Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(sim): the closed check counts every edge not on two facets (#4122)\n\nopen_edges counts only odd edges, so an edge on four or six facets passed\nas closed. The dual mesh of a cube smaller than a cell was three flat fins\non one edge (volume 0, no odd edge); extract_with returned it and the\nexport would have written it. iso::unpaired_edges counts every edge not on\nexactly two facets after the 1e-9 weld (a collapsed facet's self-edge\nalways counts); extract_with's dual fallback and stock_export's refusal\nread it. open_edges stays for its other callers.\n\nPins (synthetic): stock_dual a_body_under_one_cell_never_panics_and_never_opens\nnow also asserts every edge on two facets and fails on the old fallback\n(1 edge); iso unit tests: two cubes on one edge pass open_edges and count\none unpaired edge; a collapsed sliver pair counts.\n\nFixes #4122\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
