      "message": "test(sim): the collapsed-facet pin reaches only the corner-to-itself rule; provenance line\n\nReview: the old fixture put both slivers on one cube edge (six facets),\nso it passed without the a == b clause. Now two facets meet at one\nwelded corner with their third corners apart: every edge is on two\nfacets, and only the edge from v to itself counts. Fails without the\nclause (left 0, right 1).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
